[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   step_094: Six-channel joint axis-permutation test (mean-plane channel added).
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   Step 069 established the joint test: the probability that a single
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   arbitrary sky direction reproduces the combined anomaly across all
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   populations and catalogues at once, evaluated by re-running every
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   channel about each of 20000 random axes.  This step adds the sixth,
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   catalogue-independent channel introduced in step 090: the fitted
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   mean-plane lean azimuth of the MPCORB non-resonant 80-400 AU sample
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   under the SCT25 likelihood estimator.
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   C6  mean-plane channel : fraction of unwarped-disk null realizations
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   whose fitted mean-plane pole azimuth lands at least as close to
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   the trial axis longitude as the observed pole azimuth does.  The
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   null pole ensemble is the position-conditioned Monte Carlo of
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   step 090 (step_b55_mean_plane.json -> bins["80-400"].null_poles),
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   so the channel inherits that step's bias-free construction.
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   All five step-069 channels are reproduced verbatim with the same seed
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   and the same axis draws, so the five-channel statistics are identical
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   and the only change is the added channel.  The combined statistic is
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   again Fisher's S = -2 sum ln p over the now six channels; the global p
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   is the fraction of random directions whose combined statistic reaches
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   the value measured at the observed axis.  Because channel 6 is drawn
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   from an independent catalogue lineage (MPC orbit solutions, not SBDB),
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   the extended test also checks whether a second fitter's population
[2026-10-16 13:40:02 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 094]   concurs on the same sky direction.
